  "initial_reflection": {
    "summary": "The run assembled powerful defensive tools, especially Impervious and Apparitions, but entered the Collector fight with only 40 maximum HP and no potions. The clearest combat error was failing to use an available Apparition while facing multiple attacks. Separately, both Sapphire Key opportunities were surrendered for relics, making a Heart-capable completion impossible even before the loss.",
    "lessons": [
      {
        "category": "COMBAT",
        "title": "Use Apparition instead of small blocks under concentrated attacks",
        "situation": "When HP is low, multiple enemies are attacking, and Apparition is legal, compare it against ordinary Defends before ending the turn.",
        "lesson": "Prioritize Apparition in this situation rather than spending energy on a few points of block. At the final fight's Turn 4 state, Apparition+ was available while both Torch Heads intended to attack, yet two Defend+ cards were played and the turn ended with only 6 block.",
        "evidence_points": [
          "Turn 4 began at 37/40 HP with 6 block and two Torch Heads both showing ATTACK; Apparition+ was a legal alternative.",
          "The agent played Iron Wave, then two Defend+ cards, and ended the turn; the final legal state still offered Apparition+ or End turn."
        ],
        "reasoning": "The logged state shows a low-health, multi-attacker situation where Apparition was available before the attacks resolved. Exact incoming damage is not recorded, but using only 6 block left substantially less protection than the available Intangible effect.",
        "confidence": "high"
      },
      {
        "category": "MAP",
        "title": "Do not trade away mandatory keys for merely good relics",
        "situation": "When a linked-relic choice offers a Sapphire Key, take the key unless the relic is essential to the run's immediate survival.",
        "lesson": "Preserve the Sapphire Key across acts when pursuing a Heart-capable run. This run surrendered it twice—first for Pantograph and later for Akabeko—so it finished Act 2 with no Sapphire Key and could not complete the three-key objective.",
        "evidence_points": [
          "Act 1 Floor 9 chose Pantograph and gave up the Sapphire Key.",
          "Act 2 Floor 26 chose Akabeko and again gave up the Sapphire Key.",
          "The final keys were ruby=False, emerald=False, sapphire=False."
