        "reasoning": "Both decisions explicitly offered the key as an alternative, and the final state confirms that the key was never recovered. The relic gains were useful but not shown to be necessary for survival, while the lost key permanently prevented the intended endgame objective.",
        "confidence": "high"
      },
      {
        "category": "EVENT",
        "title": "Treat large maximum-HP sacrifices as a build commitment",
        "situation": "Before accepting a reward that removes a large fraction of maximum HP, verify that the deck already has enough defensive synergy and that future fights can exploit the reward.",
        "lesson": "Accepting five Apparitions for a 40-max-HP loss can be powerful, but it creates very little margin for mistakes. After taking it, prioritize intangible timing and avoid relying on ordinary Defends to survive multi-enemy attacks.",
        "evidence_points": [
          "At Act 2 Floor 24, the run accepted five Apparitions and lost 40 maximum HP, falling from 74/80 to 40/40.",
